---
import {
	GITHUB_PROFILE_URL,
	HOMELAB_REPOSITORY_URL,
	SITE_TITLE,
} from '../consts';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const description =
	'About Stephen McCruden: field engineering, Kubernetes, infrastructure automation, observability, and reliable systems.';
---

<BaseLayout title={`About | ${SITE_TITLE}`} description={description}>
	<main id="main-content" class="page">
		<header class="about-hero">
			<div class="about-intro">
				<p class="eyebrow">About me</p>
				<h1>I turn operational experience into better systems.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					I’m Stephen McCruden, a field engineer focused on reliable
					infrastructure, automation, and the disciplined work required
					to keep important systems running.
				</p>
			</div>

			<aside class="profile-card surface" aria-label="Professional snapshot">
				<div class="profile-mark" aria-hidden="true">SM</div>
				<dl>
					<div>
						<dt>Role</dt>
						<dd>Field Engineer</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Domain</dt>
						<dd>Mission-critical communications</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Focus</dt>
						<dd>Infrastructure & reliability</dd>
					</div>
					<div>
						<dt>Region</dt>
						<dd>Washington, D.C. area</dd>
					</div>
				</dl>
			</aside>
		</header>

		<section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="work-title">
			<div class="section-index">
				<span>01</span>
				<p>Professional work</p>
			</div>
			<div class="story-copy">
				<h2 id="work-title">Reliability starts before the incident.</h2>
				<p>
					I support mission-critical public-safety communications
					infrastructure. My work includes system upgrades, lab
					validation, troubleshooting, documentation, and coordinating
					technical work across teams and customer environments.
				</p>
				<p>
					That environment has shaped how I approach engineering:
					understand the dependencies, document the procedure, validate
					the result, and prepare for what happens when something fails.
					A system is only as reliable as the people, processes, and
					recovery paths around it.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="story-section" aria-labelledby="lab-title">
			<div class="section-index">
				<span>02</span>
				<p>The homelab</p>
			</div>
			<div class="story-copy">
				<h2 id="lab-title">A lab for practicing the full operating model.</h2>
				<p>
					My primary engineering project is a three-node Kubernetes
					platform running on Proxmox. It is a reproducible environment
					for infrastructure engineering—not simply a collection of
					self-hosted applications.
				</p>

				<div class="lab-stack">
					<article>
						<span>Provision</span>
						<strong>Terraform defines the virtual infrastructure.</strong>
					</article>
					<article>
						<span>Configure</span>
						<strong>Ansible builds and hardens every node.</strong>
					</article>
					<article>
						<span>Operate</span>
						<strong>Flux reconciles the platform from Git.</strong>
					</article>
					<article>
						<span>Observe</span>
						<strong>Prometheus and Grafana expose behavior.</strong>
					</article>
				</div>

				<p>
					The cluster has been destroyed and rebuilt without
					undocumented manual intervention. Ongoing work expands
					storage, centralized logging, disaster recovery, application
					delivery, and deliberate failure testing.
				</p>

				<a
					class="text-link"
					href={HOMELAB_REPOSITORY_URL}
					target="_blank"
					rel="noreferrer"
				>
					Explore the homelab repository
					<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
				</a>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="principles-section" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
			<div class="section-heading">
				<p class="eyebrow">Engineering principles</p>
				<h2 id="principles-title">How I decide what “done” means.</h2>
			</div>

			<div class="principles-grid">
				<article class="surface">
					<span>01 / Reproducibility</span>
					<h3>Recovery should be executable.</h3>
					<p>
						If a system cannot be reconstructed predictably, its
						recovery process is incomplete.
					</p>
				</article>
				<article class="surface">
					<span>02 / Observability</span>
					<h3>Healthy-looking is not enough.</h3>
					<p>
						System behavior and failure signals need to be visible
						before a decision can be trusted.
					</p>
				</article>
				<article class="surface">
					<span>03 / Documentation</span>
					<h3>Knowledge should survive handoff.</h3>
					<p>
						Architecture decisions, procedures, and incident lessons
						should outlive the person who found them.
					</p>
				</article>
				<article class="surface">
					<span>04 / Validation</span>
					<h3>Trust follows testing.</h3>
					<p>
						Backups, automation, and high availability become
						credible only after the failure path is exercised.
					</p>
				</article>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="toolkit-section" aria-labelledby="toolkit-title">
			<div class="section-heading">
				<p class="eyebrow">Working toolkit</p>
				<h2 id="toolkit-title">Technologies I use to build and operate.</h2>
			</div>

			<div class="toolkit surface">
				<div>
					<span>Systems</span>
					<ul class="tag-list">
						<li class="tag">Linux</li>
						<li class="tag">Proxmox</li>
						<li class="tag">Networking</li>
						<li class="tag">Containerd</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div>
					<span>Automation</span>
					<ul class="tag-list">
						<li class="tag">Terraform</li>
						<li class="tag">Ansible</li>
						<li class="tag">GitHub Actions</li>
						<li class="tag">Python</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div>
					<span>Platform</span>
					<ul class="tag-list">
						<li class="tag">Kubernetes</li>
						<li class="tag">Cilium</li>
						<li class="tag">Flux</li>
						<li class="tag">Traefik</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div>
					<span>Reliability</span>
					<ul class="tag-list">
						<li class="tag">Prometheus</li>
						<li class="tag">Grafana</li>
						<li class="tag">Runbooks</li>
						<li class="tag">Failure testing</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="direction surface" aria-labelledby="direction-title">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">What comes next</p>
				<h2 id="direction-title">Building toward platform and site reliability engineering.</h2>
				<p>
					This site documents that progression honestly: the
					architecture, implementation, failures, recoveries, and
					decisions behind the finished systems.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="direction-actions">
				<a class="button button-primary" href="/projects">View my work</a>
				<a
					class="button button-secondary"
					href={GITHUB_PROFILE_URL}
					target="_blank"
					rel="noreferrer"
				>
					GitHub profile
					<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
				</a>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about-hero {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(18rem, 0.65fr);
		gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
		align-items: end;
		margin-bottom: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 8rem);
	}

	.about-intro h1 {
		max-width: 12ch;
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}

	.about-intro .lede {
		max-width: 43rem;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 2vw, 1.25rem);
	}

	.profile-card {
		padding: 1.25rem;
	}

	.profile-mark {
		display: grid;
		width: 4rem;
		height: 4rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		place-items: center;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-accent-border);
		border-radius: 1rem;
		background: var(--color-accent-soft);
		color: var(--color-accent);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	.profile-card dl {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.profile-card dl div {
		padding: 0.8rem 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
	}

	.profile-card dl div:last-child {
		border-bottom: 0;
	}

	.profile-card dt {
		color: var(--color-text-subtle);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.64rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.07em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.profile-card dd {
		margin: 0.15rem 0 0;
		color: var(--color-text);
		font-size: 0.88rem;
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	.story-section {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(10rem, 0.4fr) minmax(0, 1.6fr);
		gap: clamp(2rem, 8vw, 7rem);
		padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 6rem);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
	}

	.section-index span,
	.section-index p {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.68rem;
	}

	.section-index span {
		color: var(--color-accent);
	}

	.section-index p {
		margin-top: 0.35rem;
		color: var(--color-text-subtle);
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.story-copy {
		max-width: 48rem;
	}

	.story-copy h2 {
		max-width: 17ch;
		margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
	}

	.story-copy > p {
		font-size: 1.02rem;
	}

	.lab-stack {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 0.7rem;
		margin: 2rem 0;
	}

	.lab-stack article {
		padding: 1rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
		background: rgba(17, 27, 36, 0.58);
	}

	.lab-stack span,
	.lab-stack strong {
		display: block;
	}

	.lab-stack span {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
		color: var(--color-accent);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.62rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.06em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.lab-stack strong {
		font-size: 0.86rem;
		line-height: 1.45;
	}

	.principles-section,
	.toolkit-section,
	.direction {
		margin-top: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 8rem);
	}

	.section-heading {
		max-width: 45rem;
		margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
	}

	.section-heading h2 {
		margin-top: 0.9rem;
	}

	.principles-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
	}

	.principles-grid article {
		padding: 1.5rem;
	}

	.principles-grid article > span {
		display: block;
		margin-bottom: 3rem;
		color: var(--color-accent);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.64rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.05em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.principles-grid h3 {
		margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
	}

	.principles-grid p {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}

	.toolkit {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		padding: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
	}

	.toolkit > div {
		padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 1.5rem 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
	}

	.toolkit > div:nth-child(odd) {
		border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border);
	}

	.toolkit > div:nth-child(even) {
		padding-right: 0;
		padding-left: 1.5rem;
	}

	.toolkit > div:nth-last-child(-n + 2) {
		border-bottom: 0;
	}

	.toolkit > div > span {
		display: block;
		margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
		color: var(--color-text-subtle);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.65rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.direction {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 3rem;
		padding: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3rem);
	}

	.direction h2 {
		max-width: 18ch;
		margin-top: 0.9rem;
		font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
	}

	.direction h2 + p {
		max-width: 42rem;
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}

	.direction-actions {
		display: flex;
		flex: 0 0 auto;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 900px) {
		.about-hero {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.profile-card {
			max-width: 30rem;
		}

		.direction {
			align-items: flex-start;
			flex-direction: column;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.story-section {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 1.5rem;
		}

		.lab-stack,
		.principles-grid,
		.toolkit {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.toolkit > div,
		.toolkit > div:nth-child(odd),
		.toolkit > div:nth-child(even) {
			padding: 1.2rem 0;
			border-right: 0;
			border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		}

		.toolkit > div:nth-last-child(2) {
			border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		}

		.direction-actions,
		.direction-actions .button {
			width: 100%;
		}
	}
</style>
